# The Vault EC2's API process — SAME codebase as infra/aws/systemd/rawprod-api.service (identical
# hardening block below), running on its own instance with its own security group, its own IAM
# role, and its own env file. Every hardening comment in rawprod-api.service applies here
# unchanged and is not repeated. UNLIKE rawprod-api.service, this unit's ExecStart runs
# `vault-main.ts`, NOT `main.ts` — see that file's own header for the full account.
#
# ── PB-03 REMAINDER: THE GAP THIS FILE'S PREVIOUS VERSION DOCUMENTED IS NOW CLOSED ──────────────
#
# The previous version of this unit ran the FULL `main.ts`/`AppModule` here, with `DATABASE_URL`
# pointed at the SAME shared `rawprod` database the main EC2 uses — because `AppModule` (via
# `BackendKernelModule.forRoot()`) unconditionally needed a main-schema Postgres connection just
# to boot (`JwtAuthGuard`/`PermissionsGuard` themselves need no DB — they verify a JWT purely off
# its claims — but `DrizzleModule`'s `PG_CLIENT` factory used to require `DATABASE_URL`
# unconditionally, and `ClusterOrgModule`'s login path does need `iam.user_master`). That was
# the shared-credential path V4 §109.1 exists to close, and this unit's own comment said so.
#
# `backend/api/src/vault-main.ts` (`VaultAppModule`) closes it: `DATABASE_URL` is not set in
# `/etc/rawprod/vault.env` AT ALL (it's optional in `config.schema.ts` now — main.ts's own
# `DrizzleModule` still fails fast if IT boots without one; `VaultAppModule` never imports
# `DrizzleModule`). This process holds ONLY `FORMULA_DATABASE_URL` (the real, isolated vault-pg,
# `ra_vault` role) — no grant, no connection string, no network path to `alembic-pg` at all.
#
# Identity without the main DB: a vault user signs in on the main app box exactly like every
# other RawProd staff member (ALEMBIC OTP -> signed assertion -> `POST /auth/alembic-assertion`,
# which mints the RawProd JWT with roles/permissions embedded) and presents that SAME JWT here;
# `JwtAuthGuard`/`PermissionsGuard`/`FreshAuthGuard` verify it off `JWT_SECRET` alone (shared with
# the main app box via SSM — never baked into either box's image). `vault-app.module.ts`'s header
# documents why this box does NOT implement its own `/auth/alembic-assertion` (it would need
# `iam.user_master` to bind the assertion to a user, i.e. exactly the credential being removed).
#
# Vault material-search / RM_ALIAS resolution (the one main-DB-SHAPED read the Vault box still
# needs): a signed, read-only proxy call to the main app box's `/internal/vault-bridge/*` routes
# (`MaterialFactsClient`, `@ra/cluster-formula`) — `INTERNAL_BRIDGE_KEY` below, never a live
# `PG_CLIENT`. The opposite direction (main app box -> Vault, resolving a coded manufacturing
# instruction for Production) is the same signed channel in reverse — `VaultPortHttpClient`
# calling THIS box's `/internal/vault/resolve-manufacturing-instruction`; the SG rule that opens
# vault-app's SG to that one port from the app box's SG is `scripts/apply-vault-port-sg-rule.sh`
# (written for P0 to review and apply — NOT run by this unit or any lane).
#
# Required in /etc/rawprod/vault.env (beyond what rawprod-api.service's env already documents):
# VAULT_MODE=true, FORMULA_DATABASE_URL, JWT_SECRET (== the main app box's, via SSM),
# FORMULA_KMS_KEY_ID (+ region — prod refuses any KMS adapter but AWS KMS), INTERNAL_BRIDGE_KEY
# (shared secret for both signed-bridge directions, via SSM), MAIN_API_INTERNAL_URL (this box ->
# main app box, material-facts bridge). DATABASE_URL must NOT be set.

[Unit]
Description=Vault API (vault-main.ts/VaultAppModule — separate trust domain, see comment above)
After=network-online.target vault-migrate.service
Requires=vault-migrate.service

[Service]
Type=exec
User=rawprod
Group=rawprod
WorkingDirectory=/srv/rawprod/app
EnvironmentFile=/etc/rawprod/vault.env
ExecStart=/opt/node-v22.12.0/bin/node --import @swc-node/register/esm-register backend/api/src/vault-main.ts

# G6: logs to a file the CloudWatch agent ships to /rawaroma/rawprod/vault-api (PID1 opens it, so ProtectSystem=strict is fine)
StandardOutput=append:/var/log/rawprod/vault-api.log
StandardError=append:/var/log/rawprod/vault-api.log
KillSignal=SIGTERM
TimeoutStopSec=30
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=5s

NoNewPrivileges=true
PrivateTmp=true
ProtectSystem=strict
ProtectHome=true
PrivateDevices=true
RestrictAddressFamilies=AF_INET AF_INET6 AF_UNIX
LockPersonality=true

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
